Hi,

sam() does not work well (yet) if you use std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE as a local
argument within mm.args(), while the 'global' model is using std.lv <http://std.lv> = FALSE.

So remove the mm.args=list() argument altogether, and directly use
std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE instead.

Still, at least a warning should be given. I opened an issue about this
on github so I don't forget.

Yves.

