From uce192d1e2170e432 at groups.google.com  Mon Jun  3 09:47:59 2024
From: uce192d1e2170e432 at groups.google.com (Emma Scandolo)
Date: Mon, 03 Jun 2024 09:47:59 +0000
Subject: Treatment effects with latent covariates: continuous vs discrete measures
Message-ID: <EA8mIAdec74.dzleVpj5BQAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/EA8mIAdec74/m/dzleVpj5BQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi everyone,

I have been trying to wrap my head around this for a while now and decided to try to get some help from the community.

I'm currently estimating the effect of a treatment (A and B) on performance scores, and I want to understand if this effect is mediated by some latent variables.

Essentially, I am estimating three different models:

1.          Base Model to Understand Treatment Effect without Mediators:

Measurement model:

Var1 =~ item1 + item2 + item3

Var2 =~ item4 + item5 + item6

Var3 =~ item7 + item8 + item9

Var4 =~ item10 + item11 + item12 + item13 + item14 + item15 + item16 + item17

Var5 =~ item18 + item19 + item20 + item21 + item22 + item23

Perf =~ measure1 + measure2 + measure3 + measure4 + measure5 + measure6

Regressions:

Perf ~ A + B

2.          Model Including Mediators in the Regression:

Measurement model:

Var1 =~ item1 + item2 + item3

Var2 =~ item4 + item5 + item6

Var3 =~ item7 + item8 + item9

Var4 =~ item10 + item11 + item12 + item13 + item14 + item15 + item16 + item17

Var5 =~ item18 + item19 + item20 + item21 + item22 + item23

Perf =~ measure1 + measure2 + measure3 + measure4 + measure5 + measure6

Regressions:

Perf ~ A + B + Var1 + Var2 + Var3 + Var4 + Var5

3.          Model Including the Impact of Treatment on Mediators:

Measurement model:

Var1 =~ item1 + item2 + item3

Var2 =~ item4 + item5 + item6

Var3 =~ item7 + item8 + item9

Var4 =~ item10 + item11 + item12 + item13 + item14 + item15 + item16 + item17

Var5 =~ item18 + item19 + item20 + item21 + item22 + item23

Perf =~ measure1 + measure2 + measure3 + measure4 + measure5 + measure6

Regressions:

Perf ~ A + B + Var1 + Var2 + Var3 + Var4 + Var5

Var1 ~ A + B

Var2 ~ A + B

Var3 ~ A + B

Var4 ~ A + B

Var5 ~ A + B

The strange thing is that in Model 1, the standardized effect of treatment A on Perf is 0.8 SD. In Model 2, it is 0.9 SD, and in Model 3, it is 0.2 SD. What doesn't make sense to me is that if, as seen in Model 3, the effect of the treatment on the mediators is positive, and the mediators in turn have a positive effect on the outcome, I would expect the coefficient of Perf in Model 2 to be lower compared to Model 1. Moreover, this issue only occurs when I specify the measures of Var1, Var2, Var3, Var4, and Var5 as categorical. When I treat them as continuous, the coefficient of A in Model 2 decreases compared to Model 1 (as I would expect).

Any insights on why this discrepancy occurs?

Thanks in advance for your help!

Emma

