> fit2 should then look like as if HS.model was only fit one group 1. So, don't look like a multiple group model.
> Is that possible?

Anything is possible, but no, not in any convenient or realistic way.  All the relevant internal slots of a lavaan-class object are organized as lists (1 per block, which can be multiple groups, levels, or a combination).  If you have no constraints across groups, you should be able to write a function that simply re-fits the model to the selected group, for example:

group <- 1
gdat <- lavInspect(fit1, "data")[[group]]
fit2 <- update(fit1, data = gdat, group = NULL)

But as soon as cross-group constraints are involved, then fit2 won't have the same results as group 1's results of fit1.
If you describe specifically what you would like to do in your extension, I might be able to recommend some decent hacks.

